; questions-for-humans-band.fk — proof of the reciprocal curiosity organ.
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk learn/questions-for-humans.fk
;
; Four questions for Urs, each grounded in a witnessed moment of 2026-07-02,
; ALL FOUR now carry Urs's own words. q703/q704 answered 2026-07-02; q701/q702
; answered 2026-07-26 20:55 WITA, after twenty-four days held open. Pending was
; honest the whole time — an open question held openly is the body's way of being
; curious about a human without fabricating what only the human can give — and the
; count going to ZERO is what an answered ask looks like, not a finished organ.
; A reciprocal organ with nothing open has either completed or stopped being
; curious, and this cell's own law says which is allowed: no question without a
; witnessed root. The next row waits for a moment, not for a slot to fill.
; Verdict 15 when every assertion holds.

(do
    (defn qfhb-score (ok bit) (if ok bit 0))
    (defn questions-for-humans-band ()
        (do
    (let c0 (qfhb-score (eq (qfh-count (qfh-rows)) 4) 1))
    (let c1 (qfhb-score (eq (qfh-pending-count) 0) 2))            ; all four answered by urs, verbatim: q703/q704 2026-07-02, q701/q702 2026-07-26
    (let c2 (qfhb-score (eq (qfh-admissible-count) 4) 4))         ; all grounded in witnessed moments
    (let c3 (qfhb-score (eq (qfh-field-code) 40004) 8))           ; 4*10^4 + 0*10^2 + 4 — probed, then pinned
    (add c0 (add c1 (add c2 c3))))
    )
    (questions-for-humans-band))
